**Gates**
- **Windows** (RTX 5080, MSVC): vendor validation, configure, `win-debug` build, `win-unit` ctest, `engine_tests --suite editor --backend dx12` (43 cases, 464 assertions), and `engine_tests --suite gpu --backend dx12` (72 cases, 43923 assertions) all exit 0.
- **Linux** (clang, debug): vendor validation, the full `linux-debug` build, and `ctest --preset linux-unit` (30 of 30) pass. `engine_tests --suite editor` passes with 42 cases, 446 assertions.
- **Not run:** `linux-gcc` (only GCC 9.4 is installed here; the physics code needs GCC 11+), `linux-asan` / `linux-sanitize`, the native Linux Vulkan editor and GPU suites, and the bench (this story doesn't touch performance-sensitive code).
- **GUI:** not verified. The Windows desktop is still locked, so no screenshots or action log exist. The Hierarchy and Inspector are compiled and built into the editor, but I have not seen them render.

**What was built**
- `SceneEditor` (`engine/editor/src/scene_editor.cpp`) has no ImGui dependency. It covers:
  - create, duplicate (copies the subtree with new GUIDs), delete (removes the subtree), reparent, and search by GUID or component type;
  - add/remove components through the reflected catalog;
  - field and transform edits validated against the descriptor, with out-of-range, non-finite, and wrong-kind values rejected;
  - save, open, and a dirty flag computed by comparing against the last saved text;
  - missing asset GUIDs shown in the inspector as "Missing asset", and a missing prefab fails to open with its GUID.
- The UI adds Hierarchy and Inspector panels, a scene file toolbar, drag-and-drop reparenting, and an unsaved-changes dialog. New, Open, Close project, Exit, and the window close button all go through that dialog.
- `Scene::component_types` is a small addition to `engine/scene`.
- `tests/src/editor_scene_tests.cpp` adds 13 CPU cases; the test-file registration is in `tests/CMakeLists.txt`.
- `docs/editor.md` and `.ralph-tui/progress.md` are updated.

**Choices I made that you may want to change**
- Delete removes the whole subtree. It has no undo.
- Reparent keeps the entity's local transform, so it moves with the new parent. It does not keep its world position.
- Rotation is edited as Euler degrees, so every typed value stays a valid unit quaternion.
- Hierarchy and Inspector are always shown and are not in the View menu. They are added to the default layout only, so an existing saved layout will not place them.
- The hierarchy lists the scene's own entities. Entities inside a prefab instance are not listed, and the editor cannot load prefab files yet.
- The scene file path is typed into the Hierarchy panel, since there is no native file dialog.
- The component catalog is empty in the shipped editor. Game code must register components before they can be added in the inspector.
